by soyuka at 2026-09-01T08:21:30Z

Thanks @wachterjohannes - you were right on both counts, and I've reworked this rather than defend the original shape.

@chr-hertel you asked the shape question back in June and it's been open since; rather than leave it sitting I've gone with the Gemini/VertexAI map shape, since that's where both of you leaned. Happy to revisit if you'd rather have pass-through plus docs.

What changed:

- `server_tools` is now a `name => params` map, mapping to Anthropic's versioned `type`, matching Gemini/VertexAI. Raw `tools` stays the escape hatch for unmapped tools and is now documented as such - including for `web_fetch`, which isn't mapped because its results aren't converted yet.
- `web_search` results are wired up. You were right that `ResultConverter` had no `web_search_tool_result` branch - a search was silently dropped, or threw when the reply had no text block. Both are now covered by tests. The call and result blocks merge into one `WebSearchResult` (query + id + status), matching how OpenResponses represents a search.
- On `cache_control`: good catch, and I didn't verify it against the live API either - so I removed the question instead of answering it. Server tools are appended after cache-control injection, so it always lands on the last function tool. There's a regression test asserting it is *not* on the server tool.
- CHANGELOG entry moved to `0.13`.
- Docs rewritten, `examples/anthropic/server-tools-web-search.php` added, and the two code-execution examples migrated to `server_tools` so they match the docs.
- Rebased fresh onto main.

One limitation I want to flag rather than bury: `WebSearchResult` has no field for individual search hits, and carrying them means changing a Platform-wide class OpenResponses also populates. Same for streaming - `convertStream()` handles text, thinking and tool calls only, so server tool blocks don't surface there. Both are noted in the RST, with follow-ups for search hits, `citations`, `encrypted_content` round-tripping, and the missing `Content\WebSearch` branch in `AssistantMessageNormalizer`.

The two red `Unit / Store / S3Vectors` checks are a pre-existing async-aws pagination failure, unrelated to this branch.

